# Yeelight bulb IPs — one per line, '#' comments allowed.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/yeelight/bulbs.txt and fill in this network's addresses:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/yeelight
#   cp bulbs.txt.template ~/.config/yeelight/bulbs.txt
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/yeelight/bulbs.txt
#
# The filled-in version is NEVER committed — dotfiles is a public repo, and a
# bulb list is an inventory of the home LAN. Same rule as ~/.config/nephos/env.
#
# Find bulbs on the local network (LAN control must be enabled in the Yeelight app):
#   python -c "from yeelight import discover_bulbs; print(discover_bulbs())"

